; A head-set name whose ONLY form is slot-local — no global declaration
; anywhere. `bgl-resource` names `storage-texture`, and the only
; `(form :name storage-texture …)` is a slot-local of `entry`, which is itself
; a slot-local of `bind-group-layout`.
;
; Head-set narrowing is byte-equality over `:names` and resolves nothing —
; not at manifest-load time, not at validate time. The descent that FOLLOWS a
; narrowed head is a separate step, and that step is local-first. So a global
; "dummy" form is not required to make a head-set name resolvable, and must
; not become required.
;
; Sibling of `positional-local-headset-resolves-local`, which keeps a global
; `entry` in place to prove *shadowing* — a local beats a same-named global.
; This case removes the global entirely to prove *sufficiency*. A refactor
; that reordered the fallback (global first, local second) would keep that
; case green and turn this one red, which is the whole point of having both.
(plugin :name p :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name bgl-entry-item :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [entry]))
  (value-kind :name bgl-resource :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [buffer storage-texture]))
  (form :name bind-group-layout
    :positional bgl-entry-item
    (key :name name :type symbol)
    (form :name entry
      :positional bgl-resource
      (key :name binding :type number)
      (form :name buffer
        (key :name type :type symbol))
      (form :name storage-texture
        (key :name format :type symbol)))))

(bind-group-layout :name bgl0
  (entry :binding 0 (storage-texture :format rgba8unorm)))
